[["heading","SECTION 23 / PRACTICAL PROJECT\nSecure Order API — test plan"],["heading","Scenario\nExpected"],["text","Valid customer login\nNew session ID"],["text","Wrong password or unknown email\nGeneric 401"],["text","Own order, valid session\n200"],["text","Other customer's order\n404 (concealment policy)"],["text","No valid session\n401"],["text","POST without valid CSRF proof\n403"],["text","Repeated excessive login attempts\n429 under configured policy"],["text","Reuse old cookie after logout\n401"],["heading","Interview rehearsal"],["text","Q: How did you secure your project? Explain only techniques you actually implemented. A\npractice answer: “I authenticate the user, then verify permissions and ownership on every protected\nendpoint. I store salted password hashes, protect sessions, validate input, and write negative\nauthorization tests.”"],["sinhala","","Jම් answer එක තමන් ඇතේතටම project එJකේ implement කරපු Jදේවල් අනුව Jවනස් කරන්න.",462],["sinhala","","Implement Jනාකළ controls දන්නවා කියලා විතරකේ පැහැදිලි කරන්න.",343],["heading","Challenge"],["text","Design a token-based alternative. Compare revocation, refresh rotation, token storage, XSS/CSRF\ntradeoffs and scaling with the session-based version. Draw the trust boundaries and list five\nnegative tests."]]